 0, Entry Helix radius 1.
 
+**Pass starts at** (Passes tab) sets where each level starts:
+
+- **Auto** cuts the rings from the middle of the area outward. This is
+  the order that 2D Offset always cut.
+- **Outside** starts at the outer edge of the area and works in. With an
+  Outside containment, the outer edge is the stock edge: the tool starts
+  outside the stock, cuts one stepover at a time and ends on the part
+  wall. Use it to stop full-width slots in the stock.
+- **Inside** starts at the part or island wall and works out.
+
 **Do not touch** (Geometry tab, **Boundaries**): pick faces or edge chains
 to protect from every cut, plunge, ramp, helix, keep-down and rapid link
 across the full tool assembly (flutes, shank and holder). **Clearance**

From 9939a6238ff087f735b93ec2a093e2bd9e35d3d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:29:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(2d): Pass start Inside/Outside walks level curves of
 one side

The second read of PR #3353 showed that the order of whole ring loops
still cut the full tool width where a ring splits at a narrow place of
the band: a split piece carries stock-side and part-side arcs.

Inside and Outside now cut level curves of the distance from the start
side only, clipped to the cutter-centre area as open pieces
(Region::clip_ring, new in geo2d/clip_line.rs). Ring 0 is the start
side of the area's own boundary, the walls come last. Pieces join only
through cut material; a re-entered piece starts with a lead-in from cut
floor. Keep-down pass links of this plan must run through cleared
columns. Each start on a wall and each full-width cut is named on the
toolpath ("Pass start" notes, warning lines on the op page). Auto keeps
the old planner byte for byte.

Refs #3316

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
